Had my first real Flame Mage (i.e. outside of discovery mode) running in
slashem and despite a very weak beginning (strength 8, a drow) and
initial difficulties (no bag) he was doing very well, the game was
beyond turn 50000, he had an AC of -18, all resistances (shock only by
ring), the Bat from Hell as a weapon and fireball spell as well as acid
stream at skilled level and 0% failure.

He died in the Wyrm caves from a rot worm, but I do not quite understand
 how.  There was no sign of illness on the status line, presumably
because he was satiated from his prior eating a black dragon. But the
terminal was at 80 characters per line and had more than the usual 24
lines, so the "satiated" message had wrapped around the bottom line, and
I know that in the past I could have several qualifiers like "satiated"
and "blind" fully written out this way. So the first question is, why
did the "ill" message not appear -- after all I had a well-enchanted
unicorn horn (and a eucalyptus leaf), so illness would not really have
been an issue. The second question is: I do not remember a rot worm
having bitten me. But shortly before dying I fell into a pit and because
I had poison resistance I did not heed the messages too much, so I might
have overlooked a message of acquring illness. Is it possible to get ill
by falling on a dead rot worm?
